Fig. 3
 shows the CBP curves from AD of FW pretreated with TPP and CTP at 50, 55, and 60°C for 6 and 12h. All the tested scenarios except for TPP at 60°C resulted in a higher biomethane production than the control. Similar to the first set of experiments, the CBP curves obtained a plateau after 20–25days of biomethanation. Hence, the experiments were stopped and the SBP was calculated for the initial 20days as well (Fig. 4
). The SBP of the control was 413.90 (±4.87) mlCH4/gVSadded, which is consistent with the previous set of experiments.
